# Go Backend

Keep packages non-overlapping. New code goes in the owning package; do not dump helpers into `api` or `kubernetes`.

```
backend/
  cmd/                 # process entry only
  internal/
    api/               # HTTP + JSON only
    websocket/         # WS accept, subscribe, broadcast
    sandbox/           # validation + lifecycle (pause/resume/delete)
    kubernetes/        # client-go calls only — no business rules
    watcher/           # register watches, fan-in, publish internally
    logs/              # open/forward/reconnect/close; multi-viewer
    resources/         # map Sandbox → Pod, PVC, Service, Events
    models/            # API/domain types
```

```go
// ❌ BAD — kubernetes package validates and knows HTTP status codes
func (c *Client) CreateSandbox(ctx context.Context, name, image string) error {
    if name == "" { return errBadRequest }
    return c.cs.Create(ctx, build(name, image))
}

// ✅ GOOD — kubernetes applies a fully formed object; sandbox service validates
func (s *Service) Create(ctx context.Context, in CreateInput) (*Sandbox, error) {
    if err := in.Validate(); err != nil { return nil, err }
    obj := s.manifest.FromCreate(in)
    return s.k8s.CreateSandbox(ctx, obj)
}
```

- `sandbox` must not import `net/http` or UI types.
- `kubernetes` must not encode product policy (defaults, UX errors, pause semantics beyond the API call).
- `watcher` is the source of list/status/delete UI updates. Use Informers/Watches, not periodic `List`.
- `resources` discovers children via **labels and OwnerReferences** only — no cluster-wide scans by name guesswork.
- `logs` owns stream lifetime: one upstream per sandbox, N subscribers, clean cancel on inspector close.
